  "notes": "One group per table row (the source tables are not subdivided), so that each prophecy member pairs with its own fulfillment; groups are ordered by the date of the fulfillment. Prophecy members are anchored per series rule 4 to the 'writing completed' record of the prophetic book (b11), except Genesis 49:10, anchored to Jacob's death (b2-0006). The jy table has 17 rows; 10 rows of the bh chart are added (its other 5 rows match jy rows and are recorded in attributes.bh_row). The ijwbq article lists about 60 prophecies; its wording for matching rows is in attributes.ijwbq_row, and its rows that neither jy nor bh have (e.g. Offspring of Abraham, Descendant of Isaac, Called by the name Immanuel, Humble beginning, Called a Nazarene, Preceded by a messenger, Anointed as Messiah in 29 C.E. (Dan. 9:25), Zealous for God's house, miracle worker and spokesman like Moses, Wonderful Counselor, Declared Jehovah's name, A Leader, Stone of stumbling, Rejected by humans, Praised by children, Came in Jehovah's name, False witnesses, Spat upon, Struck on the head, Flogged, Did not resist, Government leaders conspired, Nailed to a stake, Counted in with sinners, Suffered for sinners, Seemed forsaken, Vinegar and gall, Entrusted spirit to God, Gave up his life, Provided the ransom, Betrayer replaced) are not included. The jy row 'Bones not broken before he dies' is copied as printed; the Tamil jy reads 'after he died'. Tamil labels are from the Tamil jy page (rows 1-17) and the Tamil bh appendix (added rows)."
}
